<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rao Chunda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1423</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rao Chunda was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> chief of Marwar who took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandore">Mandore</a> around 1395 and made it the capital of his growing realm. He extended Rathore power across much of the Marwar region, but was killed in fighting around Nagaur in the 1420s. His grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rao-jodha">Rao Jodha</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jodhpur">Jodhpur</a> in 1459.</p></div>
